U,kBA=[0,cn,[0,g,bbf]],kBB=eQ,kBC=[0,cf,[0,g,eQ]],kBD="\nPlaces the **statics** refractor on the bindings at the given paths: a GUI type-ascription overlay (offside type cell) for human-readable types on expressions.\nThis does not change program text. If a runtime probe is on the same binding, it is replaced by statics (same transition as the editor\xe2\x80\x99s statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics are placed so overlays are visible.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings\n\nSee the system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** for how statics relate to probes and livelits.\n",kBE=[0,[0,lg,[0,U,[0,[0,cf,[0,g,jM]],[0,[0,ku,[0,U,[0,[0,lt,[0,U,[0,ppa,po$]]],0]]],[0,[0,h4,[0,h,[0,[0,g,lt],0]]],0]]]]],0],kBF=dU,kBG=[0,cn,[0,g,bcx]],kBH=eQ,kBI=[0,cf,[0,g,eQ]],kBJ="\nRemoves **only** the statics refractor from the bindings at the given paths.\nRuntime probes on the same binding are left unchanged (unlike remove_probe).\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to clear statics overlays from\n",kBK=[0,[0,lg,[0,U,[0,[0,cf,[0,g,jM]],[0,[0,ku,[0,U,[0,[0,lt,[0,U,[0,ppc,ppb]]],0]]],[0,[0,h4,[0,h,[0,[0,g,lt],0]]],0]]]]],0],kBL=dU,kBM=[0,cn,[0,g,bio]],kBN=eQ,kBO=[0,cf,[0,g,eQ]],kBP="\nToggles the statics refractor on or off for the bindings at the given paths (same behavior as the editor statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics end up enabled.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to toggle\n",kBQ=[0,[0,lg,[0,U,[0,[0,cf,[0,g,jM]],[0,[0,ku,[0,U,[0,[0,lt,[0,U,[0,ppe,ppd]]],0]]],[0,[0,h4,[0,h,[0,[0,g,lt],0]]],0]]]]],0],kBR=dU,kBS=[0,cn,[0,g,beS]],kBT=eQ,kBU=[0,cf,[0,g,eQ]],kBV=[0,0,0],kB5=[0,1],kB4=G,kB3=G,kB2=G,kB1=m,kB0=cz,kBZ="Printer.add_indent: Not_found",kB6=[0,m],kB7=[0,iH],kB9=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],kB_=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],kB$=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],kCa=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],kCb=[0,"- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Custom livelit projector for structured literal editing."],kCc=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],kCd=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],kCe=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],kCf=[0,0,0],kCg=[0,m,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],kCh=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],kCj=[0,m,0],kCk=[0,m,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,m,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,m,0]]]]]]]]],kCl=kx(["## Projectors and the agent view",m,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",m,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",m,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",m]),kCn=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],kCt=[0,m],kCs="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",kCr="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",kCq="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",kCo="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",kCA=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],kCz=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],